.TH VEEJAY-DIRECTOR 1 "August 2026" "VeeJay" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
veejay-director \- manage, discover, connect, route and launch VeeJay instances
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B veejay-director
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ SHOW.vjd ]
.PP
.B veejay-director
.BR \-\-discover
.PP
.B veejay-director
.BR \-\-resume
.RI [ \-\-patchbay ]
.PP
.B veejay-director
.BR \-\-show
.I FILE
.RI [ \-\-patchbay ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B veejay-director
is the multi-instance control, routing and deployment interface for VeeJay.
It can manage local VeeJay processes, connect to already running instances,
discover VeeJay engines on the LAN, configure video routes, manage projection
and output layouts, and supervise a complete multi-engine show from one
interface.
.PP
A Director show is stored in a
.B .vjd
file.  A show can contain standalone, program and output instances together
with their routing, startup, display, projection and recovery configuration.
.PP
When started without command-line arguments,
.B veejay-director
opens the
.B Start Director
window.  From there a user can create a predefined setup, open or resume a
show, or choose
.B Discover & connect
to find running VeeJay engines on the LAN.
.PP
The discovery workflow opens
.B Stage \(-> Wiring
(the patchbay) and automatically attaches advertised VeeJay instances so they
can be inspected and connected.
.SH STARTUP MODES
.TP
.B Plain startup
Running
.B veejay-director
without arguments opens the
.B Start Director
window.
.TP
.B Discovery startup
.B \-\-discover
starts LAN discovery, connects to discovered VeeJay instances and opens the
Wiring patchbay.
.TP
.B Resume startup
.B \-\-resume
opens the most recently saved or opened Director show.
.TP
.B Explicit show
.BI \-\-show " FILE"
opens the specified
.B .vjd
show directly.
.TP
.B Setup chooser
.B \-\-setup
forces the
.B Start Director
window even when using an explicit command-line startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-discover
Discover and connect to all running VeeJay instances advertised on the LAN,
then open
.B Stage \(-> Wiring
in patchbay mode.
.TP
.B \-\-connect-all
Alias for
.BR \-\-discover .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-resume
Resume the last saved or opened Director show.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-setup
Open the
.B Start Director
setup chooser.
.TP
.BR \-f " FILE" ", " \-\-show " FILE"
Open a Director
.B .vjd
show at startup.
.TP
.B \-\-patchbay
Open
.B Stage \(-> Wiring
after startup.  This can be combined with
.B \-\-show
or
.BR \-\-resume .
Discovery mode enables patchbay startup automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-no-discovery
Disable VeeJay LAN discovery for the current Director session.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display command-line help and exit.
.SH OPTION INTERACTIONS
The primary startup modes
.BR \-\-discover ,
.BR \-\-resume ,
.BR \-\-setup
and
.B \-\-show
are mutually exclusive.
.PP
.B \-\-discover
and
.B \-\-no-discovery
cannot be used together.
.PP
.B \-\-patchbay
is a view-selection option and may be combined with a direct show or resume
startup.
.SH DISCOVERY AND PATCHBAY
VeeJay LAN discovery listens for VeeJay advertisements on UDP port 3499.
Discovered engines are shown in the
.B LAN discovery
area and can be opened directly in the Wiring patchbay.
.PP
The patchbay presents VeeJay engines and available video transports as a
graph.  It is used to connect and disconnect native VeeJay routes and NDI
sources, inspect live routing state, and arrange the visual topology of a
show.
.PP
For native routing, Director may select shared memory for same-host
connections and TCP for network connections.  NDI routing is available when
VeeJay was built with NDI support and a compatible NDI runtime is available.
.SH MANAGED INSTANCES
Director can launch and supervise local VeeJay processes.  Each configured
instance has a role:
.TP
.B Standalone
An independent VeeJay engine.
.TP
.B Program
A source/program engine intended to feed one or more downstream outputs.
.TP
.B Output
An output/rendering instance consuming a configured source.
.PP
Director can also connect to unmanaged VeeJay instances that were started
outside Director.  Remote instances are controlled but are not launched or
terminated by Director.
.SH SHOW FILES
Director show files use the
.B .vjd
suffix.
.PP
A show may be opened with
.BR \-\-show ,
as a positional
.I SHOW.vjd
argument, through the desktop environment, or from the Director user
interface.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/veejay/director/state.ini
Director session state.  The most recently saved or opened show is recorded
here for
.BR \-\-resume .
.TP
.I ~/.config/veejay/director/templates/
User-defined Director setup templates.
.TP
.I ~/.veejay/director/<instance-id>/
Default working directory for Director-managed VeeJay instances.
.TP
.I *.vjd
VeeJay Director show files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NDI_RUNTIME_DIR_V6
Overrides the directory searched for the NDI runtime when NDI support is
enabled.
.PP
Director also uses the standard GTK, GLib and desktop environment variables
that affect display selection, configuration paths and the graphical session.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open the startup chooser:
.PP
.nf
.RS
veejay-director
.RE
.fi
.TP
Discover all running VeeJay engines and open the patchbay:
.PP
.nf
.RS
veejay-director \-\-discover
.RE
.fi
.TP
Resume the previous show:
.PP
.nf
.RS
veejay-director \-\-resume
.RE
.fi
.TP
Open a show directly:
.PP
.nf
.RS
veejay-director \-\-show venue.vjd
.RE
.fi
.TP
Open a show directly in the patchbay:
.PP
.nf
.RS
veejay-director \-\-show venue.vjd \-\-patchbay
.RE
.fi
.TP
Open a show without LAN discovery:
.PP
.nf
.RS
veejay-director \-\-show venue.vjd \-\-no-discovery
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
Director uses VeeJay's control protocol to inspect and control connected
engines.  Some features, including NDI, projection mapping, camera calibration
and specific output transports, depend on the capabilities of the connected
VeeJay build and host system.
.PP
For a single-engine interactive VeeJay session, see
.BR reloaded (1).
For VeeJay server options, see
.BR veejay (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR veejay (1),
.BR reloaded (1)
